Section 27: Proof of execution of documents by comparison with the original

The execution of a document may be proved by the following methods, either by itself or in conjunction with any other method, as follows:—

		By its execution by the person executing it, or by his power, or by his habit or custom, or by the course of conduct, or by the course of events, from which the execution of the document by such person is to be inferred;
		By the voice of the person executing it, or of any person acquainted with the execution of the document, or by the handwriting of the person executing it, or of any person acquainted with the handwriting of the person executing it, or by the chemical process of identifying the handwriting of the person executing it;
